<title>AUSTRALIA: Merrill appoints new Australasia debt-market chief.</title>
<headline>Merrill appoints new Australasia debt-market chief.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. investment bank Merrill Lynch on Friday announced a new managing director for Australian and New Zealand debt markets under a management realignment.</p>
<p>Keith Bailey, who now runs Merrill's U.S. dollar derivatives book, has been appointed managing director, debt markets, for Australasia, it said.</p>
<p>The appointment comes as Merrill splits management of debt markets into three broad areas -- global business, client business and global function, Merrill said.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 61-3 9286-1421</p>
